<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Larry — Stefano Passeri</title>

  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../style/reset.css" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../style/base.css" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../style/main.css" />
  
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Work+Sans:wght@300;400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href="../favicon.png">
</head>

<body>
  <div class="wrapper">
    
    <!--nav sidebar now lives in partials/nav - JS snippet at bottom fetches index for each page-->
    <nav class="sidebar" id="site-nav"></nav>

    <main class="project-display">
      <div class="project-content">

        <!--top of page-->
        <h2>Larry</h2>
        <p class="project-blurb">
          Mixed-media sculpture.
        </p>

        <!--hero image-->
        <div class="hero-image project-hero is-photo">
          <img src = "../images/larry/larry-hero.jpg" alt="Larry hero">
        </div>

        <hr class="project-hr" />

        <p class="project-blurb">
          Larry is a mixed-media sculpture wherein a cubic volume endlessly wanders within a 
          larger translucent box without ever fully aligning with it. A concealed mechanism causes 
          the interior object to move in small, intermittent shifts — a seemingly aimless, strangely 
          overperforming printer-like stutter followed by long periods of stillness and occasional 
          longer transitions. The translucent outer form maintains a familiar monolithic composure, 
          but over time the internal motion introduces subtle misalignments between appearance and behavior. 
          What seems a stable and familiar form on a cursory glance is, in fact, continually adjusting 
          and never settling.
        </p>


        <!--video-->
        <div class="project-image image-free is-photo gap-lg">
          <video 
            src="../images/larry/larry-clip-2.mp4"
            autoplay
            muted
            loop
            playsinline
            class="project-video">
          </video>
        </div>

        <div class="project-image image-free is-photo gap-lg">
          <video 
            src="../images/larry/larry-clip-1.mp4"
            autoplay
            muted
            loop
            playsinline
            class="project-video">
          </video>
        </div>

        <p class="caption">Larry's endless walk. The walk is always different, 
          but all versions are equally purposeless. </p>

        <!--img-->
        <div class="project-image image-free is-photo gap-md">
          <img src = "../images/larry/larry-img-1.jpg" alt="Larry image">
        </div>

        <p class="caption">Assembled interior CNC mechanism. </p>

        <!--video-->
        <div class="project-image image-free is-photo gap-lg">
          <video 
            src="../images/larry/larry-clip-3.mp4"
            autoplay
            muted
            loop
            playsinline
            class="project-video">
          </video>
        </div>

        <p class="caption">Detail of the motor / coupler / limit switch assembly. </p>


        <!--p5js sketches-->
        <div class="p5-row gap-lg">
          <div id="sketch1" class="p5-container"></div>
          <div id="sketch2" class="p5-container"></div>
          <div id="sketch3" class="p5-container"></div>
          <div id="sketch4" class="p5-container"></div>
        </div>

        <p class="caption">Diagrams visualizing the algorithm that controls Larry’s movement. </p>

      </div>
    </main>
  </div>

    <!--JS snippets that fetches the index for each page-->
  <script>
  fetch('../partials/nav.html')
    .then(response => response.text())
    .then(data => {
      document.getElementById('site-nav').innerHTML = data;
    });
</script>

  <!-- p5 library -->
  <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/p5@1.9.0/lib/p5.min.js"></script>

  <!-- your sketch -->
  <script src="../script/larry-walk.js"></script>

</body>
</html>
